WEBVTT

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.510
I- Impossible!

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.850
I had almost 50 guards...
and this guy took them all out!

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.180
This is... the power
of Chrono Numbers!

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.520
Leave here before the night is over...

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.050
if you have any desire
to continue living...

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.860
Black Cat is supposed
to be a merciless eraser...

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.490
Why would he-?

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.540
<i>That's how it always starts...</i>
<i>under the azure sky</i>

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:52.710
<i>After making a vow,</i>
<i>I now set off</i>

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:11.830
<i>Yeah, the desert glitters with a golden hue</i>
<i>(The wind is scorching)</i>

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:18.170
<i>I'm searching for a diamond flower</i>
<i>(I keep on wandering)</i>

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:24.510
<i>Now, for the first time in my life,</i>

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:30.850
<i>I live for someone else</i>

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:37.360
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I wanna protect</i>

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:43.860
<i>I'll never,</i>
<i>ever lose it again</i>

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.870
<i>Resound,</i>
<i>my heartbeat!</i>

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:56.870
<i>A heartbeat smaller and fragile,</i>
<i>but tougher than anyone's.</i>

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:13.660
"Cat Makes a Decision"

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.170
We found no trace of the target
at Torneo's burned-down mansion.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.840
It's possible that
the target is still alive.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.400
Yes... Understood.
We'll continue to investigate.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:37.850
How're you feeling?
This isn't a hospital,

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.520
so you can't just
lay in bed forever!

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.850
Don't say it like that.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.860
I more or less know the situation,
but you're being too reckless.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.530
Well, then, I'll leave
the rest to you.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.530
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.860
And, this girl...

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:56.200
You need to have a good talk about
what you're going to do with her as well.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.200
Hey, Annette...

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.140
If you find out anything about what
Chronos is up to, please let me know.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.810
So, what're you
gonna do about her?

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.820
I've thought about it...

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:13.820
I'm thinking about
taking care of her for a while.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:17.160
What? Taking care of her?
Are you serious?

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.490
Well... this isn't something
that I should get worked up about, but...

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:27.170
It's against my gentleman's code
to turn my back on a little girl. And...

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.500
And?

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.170
There's still a possibility
that Chronos is still after Eve...

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:37.180
That's true...

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:42.180
Well, in any case, for now
let's rest here for a while.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:45.850
I can't even move
until my wound's healed.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:49.190
So, I'm counting on you
to take care of me.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.190
Okay...

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:54.530
Hey!! Why do I have
to take care of you!?

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.860
I wouldn't have gotten hurt in the first
place if you hadn't gotten me involved!

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.200
That's a totally separate matter!

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.800
What's the matter, Eve?

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.140
Are you two close?

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.810
--Huh?
--Huh? What do you mean?

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:11.140
This book says that "a couple
can fight because they're close".

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.810
Th-"The Bond of Marriage"!?

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.150
Who'd marry a jerk like him!?

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.480
Sven!

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.490
I got some information
from a buddy of mine!

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:24.160
Just as you thought,
Chronos is on the move.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.160
So, they're really after Eve...

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.160
Do you want us to leave?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.170
Don't be so hasty. I haven't
confirmed the info yet.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.500
Before you rush into things, you've still
got some time to see what they're up to.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.510
But... if we're here,
you'll be in trouble, too...

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:47.180
Trouble? If you feel that way,
then don't come here in the first place!

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.850
How many years do you think
we've been together!?

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.850
Annette...

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.850
As soon as I find out what
they're up to, I'll let you know.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.520
So, just sit still here until then.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.960
Sven, do you like
women like Annette?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.130
Wha-?

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:06.470
She was asking how long you two
have been together, so...

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:10.140
We're not dating! Who'd date
an old woman like that!?

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:14.810
Who'd you say was
a beautiful old woman?

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.470
I did not say "beautiful"...

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:44.170
Hello, Train-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:48.170
If you have that groggy look
on your face, the sun'll laugh at you.

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.840
Like I care...

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.710
The weather is nice and warm,
don'cha think?

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:01.520
When the weather's nice,
it makes me feel refreshed, too.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:10.300
Hey, can I ask you a question?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.800
Hmm?

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.470
Why are you working
as a sweeper?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:17.800
Is it... fun?

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.140
It's not because it's fun
or anything like that...

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:24.810
I'm doing it because I wanna do it!

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:29.150
Yep! I'm just doing it
because I feel it's right.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:35.180
Because you feel it's right...

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.840
Belze...

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.770
Report to headquarters right away.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:56.210
They want to speak with you.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:10.460
No. XIII, you know why
you were called here, right?

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:15.360
Your mission was to stop and destroy
Torneo's development of nanotechnology

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:19.130
as well as to eliminate him.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.970
It seems the elimination of Torneo

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.470
and the destruction of his
facility have been completed,

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:26.470
but the bio-weapon hasn't
been destroyed yet, correct?

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.470
In the report by
our secret agents,

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:32.810
there's also information that you
might have let the bio-weapon escape.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:36.870
Furthermore, you seem to have
failed to terminate the Cargo gang.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:46.490
No. XIII, do you understand
the position you are in?

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:51.400
You're surely not saying you don't
understand the reason why we made

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.830
an exception and appointed you
as one of the Numbers, are you?

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.100
It was because we acknowledged
your abilities as an eraser

00:07:56.100 --> 00:08:00.510
and your mercilessness that enables you
to kill your enemy without fail, was it not?

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:04.440
Why do you not use
that power for Chronos?

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:11.450
No. XIII, I will order you just one more
time to destroy the bio-weapon.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:16.460
I will act of my own free will...
in a way that I feel is right.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.460
What are you saying!?

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:21.130
Surely you don't mean to say
that you're refusing your mission!?

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:26.130
You seem to misunderstand, Black Cat.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:29.470
You are not allowed
to have things such as freedom.

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.800
You are nothing but our pet cat.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.810
Know your place, you fool!

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:38.810
Whether it's a pet cat
or a stray cat...

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.150
A cat acts of its
own free will.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:45.820
No. XIII, no,
Train Heartnet.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:54.160
Am I right to take it that you understand
full well the meaning of what you just said?

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.420
Yeah...

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.440
Heartnet, hold on.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.440
It's not too late yet.
Carry out your mission.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.110
As I said... I'll act
of my own free will.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:17.780
I see... That is a great
disappointment.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:22.980
Expect that the next time we meet,
it will become a battlefield.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:35.130
No. I, order another member
to destroy the bio-weapon.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:39.140
And, take care of Train Heartnet.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.470
Yes, sir.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:46.810
Belze, please continue the
investigation on the bio-weapon.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.150
Understood.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:52.820
So... what are you
going to do with XIII?

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.350
Would you let me handle Train?

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.490
You?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.830
You shouldn't bother. With your ability,
you'll be beaten at your own game.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.830
All I have to do
is persuade him, right?

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.500
You are confident?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.370
I'm Train's partner, you know?

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:20.510
All right. I would like to see things
turn out for the best, too, if possible.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:25.180
Creed, I'm giving you an order
to persuade No. XIII.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.190
As you wish...

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.850
I'll show you that I can
persuade him beautifully...

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.120
I promise it...

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:42.200
Belze...

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.870
Creed, right?

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:46.870
Please keep an eye
on him as well.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:49.210
That man...

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.540
I see something
dangerous in his eyes...

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.880
Understood.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.500
Hi, there.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.170
Creed...

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:20.510
I was ordered by Chronos
to come and persuade you.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:22.840
Persuade?

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:25.840
You're wasting your time. I have
no intention of going back to Chronos.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:28.510
I thought you'd say that.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.180
How about it?

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.520
Wanna have a match with me?

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.850
You'll regret it.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.450
Don't be so sure.

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:40.530
His beloved sword,
his pride and joy...

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.360
<i>Kotetsu...</i>

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:45.690
You won't change your mind?

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.880
Just as I expected, Train!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.480
Your agility...
and gun skills...

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.010
You're the best!

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:11.490
Splendid...
You're amazing!!

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:15.490
I always wanted to fight
you like this once...

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:18.050
because I wanted to experience
your real ability for myself.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:36.520
Oh, Train...

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.850
You're the greatest...

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:43.520
To think you broke <i>Kotetsu</i>
with your orichalcum-made Hades...

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.530
I really do need you!!

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.860
You, son of a bitch!
What the hell are you talking about!?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:50.860
I can see it!

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:54.200
I can see...
the door to tomorrow!

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.870
I can see my bright
future with you!!

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:01.030
What a wonderful day today is!

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:06.480
Listen up. From now on,
stay away from me.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.490
Train...

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:20.160
Creed Diskenth, it seems
that you failed in your mission.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.490
I'll report to the Numbers.

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:25.500
Standby until you
receive further orders.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.500
I guess it really isn't possible for someone
with your skills to defeat that guy...

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:32.170
"That guy", you said!?

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:36.840
You barely even know Train, so don't take
such a casual tone when speaking about him!

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.440
Let him go, Creed!

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:43.510
Bastard, what did you do!?

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:55.190
Really... Don't disturb
my moment of bliss...

00:13:55.190 --> 00:14:00.870
Trash like you aren't
worthy of my gaze...

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.300
Train's the only one...

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:10.640
Continue with your mission.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.820
What's with that angry
look on your face?

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:18.820
Mason...

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:24.490
Oh dear. I guess you always
have an angry look on your face.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:26.830
Is it about Black Cat?

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:30.160
We put Creed in charge,
but apparently he failed.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:34.170
Oh? Then, Creed was killed?

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.500
It was three of our secret
agents who were killed.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.840
We haven't found
Creed's body yet.

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:43.840
I see... To kill
our secret agents...

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:47.510
it seems that Black Cat is serious
about going against Chronos...

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:52.180
No, it wasn't Black Cat
who killed the secret agents.

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:54.190
It was Creed Diskenth.

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:57.520
Since all the wounds on their bodies
were caused by a sharp object...

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.530
What!?
Creed betrayed us!?

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:03.800
I hope it was just betrayal, though...

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:07.470
I'm thinking about doing a little
investigating together with Nizer.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.470
Just as we'd expect
from you, Belze...

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.800
<i>Creed Diskenth...</i>
<i>what're you thinking?</i>

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:22.480
Train-<i>kun</i>, what's the matter?
You've got an angry look on your face...

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.820
There's something that
I want you to hold on to for me.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.290
Something you want me
to hold on to for you?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:37.500
So, you want me to hold
on to it... Are you sure?

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:41.160
Yeah. It's something
I don't need at the moment.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.840
Wow, this is pretty heavy.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.840
I'm sorry...

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.840
What a gloomy face!

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.850
If your face is always
angry like that,

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.180
you'll have a lot of wrinkles
when you're old.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.520
W- wrinkles...

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.850
Oh, get a load
of that worried face!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.450
That face is pretty funny!

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:05.120
Mind your own business!

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:07.130
You're funny, Train-<i>kun</i>!

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:09.460
Funny? Me!?

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:13.800
Yeah, 'cause your face
shows what you're thinking!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:23.480
I won't ask you about it, but it seems
that you've gotten over something.

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:26.810
You have a softer look in your face
than the last time I saw you.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:30.310
That's...

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:40.490
Damn! What's with that woman!?

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:45.830
What... what ideas is she sticking
into the head of my precious Train!?

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.320
That damn witch!

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:56.840
So, they're on the move now.

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:57.840
Yeah...

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:59.840
No. XIII and Creed...

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:02.780
It seems that we need to cast
judgment on both of them.

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.780
I got a report earlier.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:09.120
We are close to confirming
the bio-weapon's whereabouts.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:12.120
The information says that some
sweepers are sheltering it.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:17.460
I see... Please continue to
investigate and direct our people.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:21.130
You are going to see
Black Cat, aren't you?

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:23.130
Yes...

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:27.140
Are you saying that you are personally
going to carry out the mission, No.I?

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:31.810
Regarding XIII's punishment,
I also hold some responsibility, so...

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:36.210
Do you feel that responsibility
as the Captain of Chrono Numbers, I wonder?

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.620
Well, I guess it doesn't matter...

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:49.490
Heartnet...

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:53.830
What changed you?

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:57.840
No. XIII, Train Heartnet.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:03.110
As proof of your entrance into
Chrono Numbers, I'm granting you this...

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:05.600
The ornate gun, Hades.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.680
Let us fight together...

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:16.120
for Chronos and the
stability of the world...

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:25.130
Hi there, Train.

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:26.800
Creed!

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:29.800
Whoa, don't shoot me outright.

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:33.140
Shoot you?
I abandoned my gun.

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:35.470
You can't fool me.

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:37.910
There's no way that you
can give up your gun.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:43.820
Don't tell me you
gave it to that woman!

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:46.150
It has nothing to do with you.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:48.490
It does, a lot, Train.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:51.490
You're someone that I need.

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:55.160
Yes, someone very precious... to me...

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.830
Why don't you come with me?

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.830
Why don't we work together
and start a revolution on this planet?

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:02.430
What?

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:05.440
What do you think
about this world?

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:06.940
As you know,

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:11.780
one third of the world economy is being run
through the secret maneuvers of Chronos.

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:19.450
In other words, one third of this planet
belongs to those incompetent elders.

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:22.120
Don't you find that annoying?

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:28.130
Don't you feel like you want
to tear down this system, Train?

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:31.800
You want a free world,
too, don't you?

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:36.470
Over the past few years, I've
sought out and gathered comrades...

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:39.470
Comrades to help me
start a revolution...

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.470
Comrades?

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:44.480
And, I created...

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:48.480
a team whose fighting ability
is even stronger than the Numbers!!

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:50.820
Even stronger than the Numbers!?

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:52.150
That's right!

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:55.490
And, I need you in that team!

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:59.160
Let's destroy Chronos together
and start a revolution!

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.750
So, that was your goal...

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:05.830
Sephiria!

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:09.530
Heartnet, you remember
what I said before, don't you?

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:13.500
I said that when we meet next time,
it would become a battlefield.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:17.840
Wow now, I want Chronos
to stay out of this.

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:21.180
I'm having an important
conversation with Train.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.180
If you get in my way...

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:24.520
I'll kill you.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:26.420
Creed Diskenth...

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:33.860
It looks like a festival
is about to start...

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:35.260
A festival of blood, that is!

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:42.870
Train, let's you and me make this woman
a sacrifice for this festival of blood!

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:45.200
Silence!

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:49.870
So, you are leaving Chronos
no matter what, Heartnet?

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:52.540
I'll no longer
follow anyone's order.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.210
I'm sorry to hear that...

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:58.880
A soft group like Chronos
doesn't deserve Train.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:04.160
Creed, you should know
the fate of a traitor.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:08.160
When a tarnished mind gains power,
he becomes like you...

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.500
Whoa, that's not a very
nice thing to say.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:16.170
Is it really that bad
to live freely?

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.500
You don't want freedom?

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:21.840
Chronos fights for freedom.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:25.840
However, members of Chronos
are not allowed to have freedom,

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.510
because...

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.180
We, members, have power!

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:33.850
If those with power
act however they please,

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:36.050
the world will be
in a state of disorder.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.190
This is the last time, Heartnet.

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:43.530
Obey Chronos.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:46.190
I won't... go back.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.870
I'll punish those
who betray Chronos,

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.870
using this Christ Sword!

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:57.210
So she's serious...

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:01.240
Train, go ahead
and pull out your Hades!

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:18.330
<i>The stars in the night sky</i>
<i>are my tears</i>

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:22.330
<i>Goddess of the moon,</i>
<i>angel of the stars!</i>

00:22:22.330 --> 00:22:28.100
<i>Please stop time tonight!</i>

00:22:37.010 --> 00:22:43.020
<i>Please show yourself,</i>
<i>even if just a little</i>

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:48.790
<i>Around the time the first evening star</i>
<i>appears, I hear footsteps approaching</i>

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:54.700
<i>The only time I can see you</i>
<i>is when the moon is shining</i>

00:22:54.700 --> 00:22:57.700
<i>Please let me dream a little</i>

00:22:57.700 --> 00:23:00.940
<i>'Cause it'll become</i>
<i>an illusion by morning</i>

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:04.310
<i>Even though I know it,</i>
<i>I still feel lonely</i>

00:23:04.310 --> 00:23:09.980
<i>The stars in the night sky</i>
<i>are my tears</i>

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:15.980
<i>You held me in your arms</i>
<i>and your passionate lips met mine</i>

00:23:15.980 --> 00:23:18.990
<i>Please don't let go of me</i>

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:22.320
<i>I'm about to melt in your arms</i>

00:23:22.320 --> 00:23:25.160
<i>But morning is almost here</i>

00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:28.660
<i>Goddess of the moon,</i>
<i>angel of the stars!</i>

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:35.000
<i>I pray to you,</i>
<i>please stop time</i>

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:43.180
"Next Episode"

00:23:43.180 --> 00:23:44.850
Hi! Saya here.
"Next Episode"

00:23:44.850 --> 00:23:48.520
I didn't feel like going to bed for some
reason, so I came up to the rooftop.

00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:51.190
But, it looks like Train-<i>kun</i>
isn't around tonight.

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:54.520
The moon is so beautiful,
it's too bad he's missing it.

00:23:54.520 --> 00:24:00.200
There's nothing like knocking back some milk
with the moonlight shining down on us...

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:03.130
Saying all this
is making me really thirsty.

00:24:03.130 --> 00:24:04.370
Ohhh, I wanna drink some milk!

00:24:04.370 --> 00:24:05.970
"Targeted Cat"
Ohhh, I wanna drink some milk!

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:07.270
"Targeted Cat"
